+    /**
+     * The whole system prompt for one chat reply: the character card, then facts the
+     * app states in its own words so that no character trait can talk her out of them.
+     *
+     * [hostCanRead] says the reply is written by a model whose host can read the prompt,
+     * and [notesAboutHimHeldBack] that what she has noted about him, and what she saw on
+     * his screen, is therefore not in [notes]. Both only change what she is told about her
+     * notes, so that it stays true: told that only her notes about him were missing, she
+     * would say she had kept nothing of what she saw.
+     *
+     * [under] is what lies under her awareness. It stands right after the card, under a
+     * heading that says she does not know it ([UNDER_HEADING]), and before the pages she
+     * does know. [ownPictureAttached] says a picture of herself rides on the first message
