+/**
+ * What the chosen rein does, worded from the code that decides it: a plan she starts
+ * runs when his own approval setting lets it, and otherwise only when her rein does.
+ * "Free on the phone" covers plans made only of actions whose whole effect stays on the
+ * phone, and no rein covers a plan whose words may be someone else's. A test holds
+ * these sentences against that code.
+ */
+internal fun reinHint(rein: PersonaRein): String = when (rein) {
+    PersonaRein.ASK ->
+        "Each thing she starts goes through the same approval setting as your own commands: what that setting " +
+            "lets run for you runs for her, and the rest is shown to you first."
+    PersonaRein.PHONE ->
+        "What stays on the phone runs at once: opening an app, pausing, skipping and the volume, an alarm or a " +
+            "timer, the light, Wi-Fi and Bluetooth, brightness, a note. What carries words off the phone goes " +
+            "through your approval setting: a message, a call, a post, a search, and playing a song by name " +
+            "too, because the name goes to a music service's search. Her command stands in the chat word for " +
+            "word before you are asked. When she wrote the command in a reply where she was shown your screen, " +
+            "or when it repeats words from a notification or from one of the app's own lines, her rein does not " +
+            "count and your approval setting decides alone, whatever the plan does."
+    PersonaRein.EVERYTHING ->
+        "Everything she starts runs at once, including messages, calls, posts and searches: what she writes " +
+            "there leaves the phone. One exception, which protects her as much as you: when she wrote the " +
+            "command in a reply where she was shown your screen, when the command repeats words from a " +
+            "notification or from one of the app's own lines, or when the plan made from it holds a number or " +
+            "an address from there that she did not write, her rein does not count and your approval setting " +
+            "decides alone. Those words may be someone else's."
+}
